WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.411
FanTake.

2
00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:03.661
Digital merch that keeps updating.

3
00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:08.196
An artist studio publishes a licensed drop, and Mo,

4
00:00:08.232 --> 00:00:10.936
a fictional demo character, opens the chat.

5
00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:13.036
He answers each fan in character.

6
00:00:14.142 --> 00:00:16.355
Then the fan decides what happens next.

7
00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:18.626
Tap a suggestion, or write your own.

8
00:00:18.662 --> 00:00:20.811
Here, she asks to stay a little longer.

9
00:00:20.847 --> 00:00:24.405
The scene is saved, and the next drop continues from her choice.

10
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.970
One drop, a different next scene for each fan,

11
00:00:29.006 --> 00:00:31.240
within options the studio approved.

12
00:00:32.346 --> 00:00:34.965
Every scene she shapes is kept in her collection.

13
00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.745
Merch that keeps updating.

14
00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:39.851
Mo remembers what each fan said.

15
00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:43.316
Tonight, she critiques his recital poster in her own words:

16
00:00:43.352 --> 00:00:46.782
the font is tiny, the colours look like expired jelly.

17
00:00:46.818 --> 00:00:50.012
He pushes back, and her feedback is saved to memory.

18
00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:54.249
Next morning, without being asked, he messages first.

19
00:00:54.285 --> 00:00:57.309
He has fixed the poster, denies it was her idea,

20
00:00:57.345 --> 00:00:59.515
and still remembers her milk-tea job.

21
00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:01.978
These are real replies from the Qwen model.

22
00:01:02.014 --> 00:01:05.166
Small achievements and stickers make it a daily habit,

23
00:01:05.202 --> 00:01:07.608
and his own life carries on between drops:

24
00:01:07.644 --> 00:01:10.924
a late alarm, and voluntary overtime on Saturday.

25
00:01:12.029 --> 00:01:13.944
Safety comes before character.

26
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.601
On a crisis message, Mo drops the act, answers gently,

27
00:01:17.637 --> 00:01:20.640
points to help, and the chat goes to human review.

28
00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:24.681
And if the filter blocks a reply, Mo sends an approved fallback line.

29
00:01:25.787 --> 00:01:27.723
The studio is the paying client:

30
00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:31.103
¥3,000 a month per IP, plus ¥8 per fan.

31
00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:36.006
In the back office, it publishes the next drop and sets the red lines.

32
00:01:37.112 --> 00:01:41.608
It sees which scenes fans chose, in aggregate only, never private chats.

33
00:01:42.714 --> 00:01:44.202
Measured, not assumed:

34
00:01:44.238 --> 00:01:48.478
under one cent per reply, and 1 serious failure in 100 tests.

35
00:01:49.214 --> 00:01:50.275
FanTake.

36
00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:53.912
Raising ¥2M for the first licensed pilot.

